      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Occoquan%2C_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The name Occoquan comes from an Algonquian word meaning 'at the end of the water'.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Occoquan%2C_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Historic Occoquan offers a self‑guided walking tour that highlights markers and stories from the town’s past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://historicoccoquan.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "River silting and the rise of railroads ended Occoquan’s days as a bustling port.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Occoquan%2C_Virginia"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Mill House Museum, run by the Occoquan Historical Society, opens daily except Wednesdays.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
